WEBVTT


00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:01.620
I've lived in both countries.

00:00:01.621 --> 00:00:05.021
Here are my opinions. Japan has electronics built for one person.

00:00:05.022 --> 00:00:06.261
People respects your space.

00:00:06.262 --> 00:00:08.381
Here in Korea, everything is done in groups.

00:00:08.382 --> 00:00:10.701
Some electronics will refuse to sit you alone in.

00:00:10.702 --> 00:00:12.661
So housing prices the worst in Tokyo.

00:00:12.662 --> 00:00:15.381
Koreans my age already gave up on buying home there.

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:17.581
Glass skin is a big part of the culture here in Korea,

00:00:17.582 --> 00:00:20.181
while Japanese skincare leans more towards a soft,

00:00:20.182 --> 00:00:21.381
fancy look. I love both,

00:00:21.382 --> 00:00:23.941
but my skin is really dehydrated and sensitive.

00:00:23.942 --> 00:00:26.801
So the glass skin approach has been a staple in my routine.

00:00:26.802 --> 00:00:30.061
One of my favourite Korean products that I always use is the 3, 4,

00:00:30.062 --> 00:00:31.901
5 lift cream from Dr Althea.

00:00:31.902 --> 00:00:34.501
It's lightweight and gentle enough for my sensitive skin,

00:00:34.502 --> 00:00:37.481
gives me lasting hydrations without clogging my pores.

00:00:37.482 --> 00:00:38.901
Whenever my skin feels stressed,

00:00:38.902 --> 00:00:40.821
it really helps calm everything down.

00:00:40.822 --> 00:00:43.101
It's perfect for Japan's hot and humid summer

00:00:43.102 --> 00:00:45.981
because it feels comfortable on the skin all day long.

00:00:45.982 --> 00:00:47.741
In Japan, if you miss the last train,

00:00:47.742 --> 00:00:49.021
you are done. In Korea,

00:00:49.022 --> 00:00:51.981
people stay out later because getting home is actually affordable.

00:00:51.982 --> 00:00:54.101
What's your favourite thing about Japan and Korea?

00:00:54.102 --> 00:00:55.321
Let me know in the comments.
